capability project-api-run-events
intent: Shape a run's events: the one declaration of the events a run stream sends, the run's trace retains and the estate live observation channel publishes, so the hosting facade composes none of them and keeps each event as answered. The facade hands it, in order, what it observed of one run since its last call: the run's admission; its start on a worker, with the kernel's pid; each observation line the run's kernel wrote, with its byte count; and the run's end, with the worker delivery's answer as it came, the kernel's closing frame for the run (null when the kernel's stream ended without one) and how many observations this capability dropped for the run; each with the time the facade observed it. It hands the end alone, after every line, together with the run as its execute-run directive declares it (runId, admittedAt, capability), the event bounds read-api-host-configuration declares (runs.events) and how many events the run holds. Each item is answered with its run event, at the run's next cursor counting from 1, or as dropped: an observation past maxEvents is dropped, and an admission, start or end is always kept. An event is {eventId urn:sfx-api:run-event:<runId>:<cursor>, cursor, at, kind, payload, rootExecutionId when its payload names one}: run.admitted {capability, admittedAt}; run.started {startedAt, pid}; run.exited {state, exitCode, endedAt, failure, droppedEvents when any were dropped, capture}, where the run completed with exit code 0 only when its delivery terminated and its result completed, and otherwise failed with exit code 1 and the first failure its delivery names (its error, its result's failure, its outcome's error), else RUN_FAILED with the disposition, and capture is the closing frame's {records, dropped}, or {complete: false} without one; an observation has the kind its observationType names, else observation, and the record as its payload, cut to {truncated: true, byteLength} with the record's observationType, testimonyType, graphId, rootExecutionId, cellId, phase and status when its line is larger than wholeObservationBytes; a line that is not JSON is observation.malformed {line}, or {truncated: true, byteLength} when it is longer than 1024 characters. Each kept item also answers the event's run stream frame (id: <cursor>, event: <kind>, data: <event>), and run.exited the run stream's end frame (event: end, data {runId, state, cursor}), which the facade writes once the run is completed. An item of any other kind is refused, RUN_OBSERVATION_KIND_UNKNOWN.
outcome: api-run-events.v1: one answer per observed item, in order, each {event, frame}, with end for run.exited, or {dropped: true}
inquiry: What are this run's events, and how does a run stream frame them?
input contract project-api-run-events-request.v1 {"type":"object","required":["run","bounds","held","observed"],"properties":{"run":{"type":"object","required":["runId"]},"bounds":{"type":"object","required":["maxEvents","wholeObservationBytes"]},"held":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"observed":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["kind","at"]}}}}
output contract api-run-events.v1 {"type":"object","required":["contractId","answers"]}
cli display outcome as json
scenario project-api-run-events root terminal
given: a run, the event bounds, the number of events it holds, and what the facade observed of it since its last call
when: each observed item is shaped into the run's next event and its run stream frame, or dropped
then: the outcome is one answer per observed item, in order
operation project-api-run-events.project kind invoke-port port project-api-run-events-project
platform bind project-api-run-events-project
platform: sda-authority-transformation-port.v1
